cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Hegemonikon
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tolmetes
    alias: tolmeton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1784-9883"
abstract: >-
  Hegemonikon is a universal cognitive architecture for AI agents in which
  perception, reasoning, and action are deduced from a single principle. Its
  axiom is the Helmholtz decomposition (Γ⊣Q); the Free Energy Principle is its
  first cognitive instance. From this it derives eight coordinates and a
  complete set of forty-eight cognitive operations, formalized in
  category-theoretic terms.
keywords:
  - free energy principle
  - active inference
  - category theory
  - cognitive architecture
  - AI agents
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tolmeton/Hegemonikon"
license: MIT
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-06-24"
